# Where a Windows build puts all five programs and shc's runtime: the
# solution builds them here and build.bat's own editor joins them, so that
# what the editor drives is beside it. None of it is this repository's.
x64/

# Visual Studio's per-user project settings. Written the first time the window
# is opened in the IDE, and nobody else's business.
*.vcxproj.user
winforms/obj/
*.pdb
*.log
gui.png
*.png

# Claude Code personal settings - never commit, holds local paths
.claude/settings.local.json

# Xcode's own build directory, when the project is built in place
build/

# What a workspace build leaves here: the two compilers and the converter
# RStudio drives, built into this directory rather than collected into it, and
# shc's runtime archives - which live beside shc because that is where shc
# looks for them. None of the four is this repository's to carry.
#
# c2s.exe was missing from this list until 2026-08-27 and sat untracked in the
# root, which is the accident a `git add -A` turns into a committed binary.
# The .dSYM bundles arrived with it: an Xcode Release build writes one beside
# each program, and `RStudio.exe` above does not match `RStudio.exe.dSYM`.
cc1.exe
shc.exe
c2s.exe
lib/
*.dSYM/

# The same build, into bin/ instead, for anyone who would rather the checkout
# stayed clean.
bin/

# A scratch file that appeared in the root and was swept into a commit by
# git add -A. It held an API key, and GitHub refused the push. Ignored so that
# it cannot happen twice.
Untitled.swift
